            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0707" n="603" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg603"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">703.94/4830: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-19T13:00:00+08:00">March 19, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 19—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Joint situation report number 11, March 19th: <pb facs="0708" n="604"
                        xml:id="pg604"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <list>
                            <item>“1. Embarkation of one Japanese mixed brigade for Japan
                                continues.</item>
                            <item>2. Commander 19th Route Army protests to neutral observers against
                                the continued flights of Japanese aircraft beyond the Shirakawa
                                patrol zone. Reports from Chinese sources that civilians have been
                                injured owing to fire from aeroplanes have not been
                                verified.”</item>
                        </list></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
